# Intended-exposure baseline — mini (Ubuntu Mac mini 192.168.10.2)
# fix-51 (fleet-sweep SM56/SM58). Consumed by bin/listener-drift.sh.
#
# Every ALL-INTERFACE (0.0.0.0 / * / [::]) TCP LISTEN port that is EXPECTED on
# mini and WHY. This is a flat-LAN homelab on the trusted VLAN: Caddy (:80/:443)
# is the auth edge, so most app ports below are 0.0.0.0 by design (docker
# publishes via docker-proxy) and are reachable direct-on-LAN — that is an
# accepted defense-in-depth tradeoff pending IoT-VLAN segmentation (ha-19).
# See wiki runbook lan-exposure.md for the model. A port that appears here but
# is NOT in this list = drift → listener-drift check FAILs (that is what would
# have caught the rogue nc -lvnp 9999 that sat here 17 days).
#
# Format: one port per line; text after # is a comment. Order irrelevant.
22      # sshd (host)
53      # adguardhome — DNS
80      # caddy — HTTP auth edge
111     # rpcbind — RPC portmapper (host)
443     # caddy — HTTPS auth edge
853     # adguardhome — DNS-over-TLS
2222    # forgejo — git SSH
3001    # uptime-kuma
3010    # homepage
3030    # forgejo — web UI
4533    # navidrome
5001    # dockge
5055    # seerr (overseerr/jellyseerr)
5230    # memos
5678    # n8n
7777    # terraria — game server
8000    # paperless-ngx
8001    # healthchecks
8010    # faster-whisper
8080    # ntfy
8081    # metube
8082    # miniflux
8085    # wallabag
8090    # beszel
8181    # tautulli
8384    # syncthing — GUI
8688    # musicseerr
8789    # libreseerr
8945    # pinchflat
8998    # romm
9000    # mealie
22000   # syncthing — sync protocol
